          sample: `The chart compares how many international tourists visited France, Spain and Thailand in four different years.

Overall, France was the most popular of the three countries throughout the period, although all three saw visitor numbers rise strongly until 2010, before falling sharply in 2020.

In 1990, France received 45 million visitors, well ahead of Spain, with 34 million, while Thailand attracted only 5 million. By 2000, France's figure had climbed to 77 million and Spain's to 46 million. Thailand's numbers doubled to 10 million, but it remained far behind the two European countries.

The following decade saw slower growth. France's total stayed almost the same, at 76 million in 2010, whereas Spain continued to rise, reaching 53 million, and Thailand grew to 16 million visitors.

In 2020, however, the pattern changed dramatically because of global travel restrictions. Numbers collapsed in all three countries: France fell to 41 million, Spain to just 19 million, and Thailand to 7 million, a lower figure than in 2000. Indeed, in 2020 none of the three countries received even half as many visitors as it had welcomed a decade earlier, and Spain suffered the largest proportional fall of all.`
