          title: "Average family spending, 1990 and 2020",
          text: "The table below shows the average monthly spending of a family, in percentages, in 1990 and 2020.\n\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\nWrite at least 150 words.",
          sample: `The table compares how an average family divided its monthly spending between different categories in 1990 and 2020.

Overall, the largest change was in food, which took a much smaller share of spending in 2020, while the proportions spent on housing, transport and leisure all increased noticeably.

In 1990, food was by far the family's biggest expense, at 38 per cent of the total. Housing was second, at 22 per cent, followed by transport at 12 per cent and clothes at 11 per cent. Leisure accounted for only 9 per cent, and other items made up the remaining 8 per cent.

By 2020, the pattern had changed significantly. Food had fallen to 24 per cent, although it was still a major cost. In contrast, housing had become the largest category, rising to 29 per cent, and transport had increased to 18 per cent. Families also spent more of their income on leisure, at 14 per cent, while the share spent on clothes dropped to just 7 per cent. Spending on other items stayed the same, at 8 per cent, the only figure that did not change at all over the thirty years.`
